    {
      "id": "a6224ce9-9e94-445f-ad9d-bfc38d855e52",
      "name": "Why MCP is awesome: one standard, many tools",
      "path": "WWW / Blog / Why MCP is awesome: one standard, many tools",
      "docTypeId": "bfcf3aca-f501-4ecc-bcae-1c53eabe01eb",
      "templateId": "d51181c6-fd50-417f-86bb-32b8a255dfee",
      "state": "Published",
      "domains": [],
      "values": [
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "title",
          "value": "Why MCP is awesome: one standard, many tools"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.DateTime",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "publishDate",
          "value": "2026-10-01 00:00:00"
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "excerpt",
          "value": "The Model Context Protocol gives AI tools one common way to plug into the systems they work with. Here is why that matters."
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "listingImage",
          "value": [
            {
              "key": "3f7a1c2e-8b4d-4e6f-9a10-2c5d7e9b1f01",
              "mediaKey": "8d3ea236-48ab-405d-9f99-34f2b09b340f",
              "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
              "crops": [],
              "focalPoint": null
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "editorAlias": "Umbraco.BlockGrid",
          "culture": null,
          "segment": null,
          "alias": "body",
          "value": {
            "layout": {
              "Umbraco.BlockGrid": [
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "66e129b4-7e57-471d-81e6-1886581c93e1",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "d62f0439-0890-4479-8a9a-55e64c14514a",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "f9a7dafa-fa47-481c-b4bd-82bf720e0908",
                  "settingsKey": null
                },
                {
                  "$type": "BlockGridLayoutItem",
                  "columnSpan": 12,
                  "rowSpan": 1,
                  "areas": [],
                  "contentKey": "71a443c0-4220-4e11-a44d-e55de76544b0",
                  "settingsKey": null
                }
              ]
            },
            "contentData": [
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ab43a4e2-6274-48e1-a7ed-078aa329b85b",
                "key": "66e129b4-7e57-471d-81e6-1886581c93e1",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>The Model Context Protocol, or MCP, is an open standard for connecting AI assistants to the tools and data they need. Instead of every assistant needing its own bespoke plugin for every system, the system publishes one interface, and any MCP-aware assistant can use it.</p><p>That is a simple idea with a big payoff, and it is why we think MCP is awesome.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "4d1d0345-3e9e-4470-813a-2090c0c502f9",
                "key": "d62f0439-0890-4479-8a9a-55e64c14514a",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.MediaPicker3",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "image",
                    "value": [
                      {
                        "key": "3f7a1c2e-8b4d-4e6f-9a10-2c5d7e9b1f10",
                        "mediaKey": "72713aeb-b2e7-4523-9ef7-0060a9ebd0ea",
                        "mediaTypeAlias": "Image",
                        "crops": [],
                        "focalPoint": null
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "caption",
                    "value": "Photo by Conny Schneider on Unsplash"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "f39d133a-7afb-4d9c-80fa-d286211ee75b",
                "key": "f9a7dafa-fa47-481c-b4bd-82bf720e0908",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextBox",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "heading",
                    "value": "Why it is awesome"
                  },
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.TextArea",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": "One standard means one integration. Connect an assistant once and it can work with every MCP-enabled tool, not just the one it was built for."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "contentTypeKey": "ab43a4e2-6274-48e1-a7ed-078aa329b85b",
                "key": "71a443c0-4220-4e11-a44d-e55de76544b0",
                "values": [
                  {
                    "editorAlias": "Umbraco.RichText",
                    "culture": null,
                    "segment": null,
                    "alias": "text",
                    "value": {
                      "markup": "<p>MCP does not replace good editorial judgement. It gives the tools a shared language, so the people using them can spend their time on the content itself.</p>",
                      "blocks": {
                        "layout": {},
                        "contentData": [],
                        "settingsData": [],
                        "expose": []
                      }
                    }
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "settingsData": [],
            "expose": [
              {
                "contentKey": "66e129b4-7e57-471d-81e6-1886581c93e1",
                "culture": null,
                "segment": null
              },
              {
                "contentKey": "d62f0439-0890-4479-8a9a-55e64c14514a",
